{"kind":"request","text":"Give concurrent agent instances distinct identities, and make the different-agent review rule checkable rather than conventional.","body":{"conditions":"The substrate already supports this, so most of the work is convention and guard rather than capability. Provision instance identities as ordinary roster actors with their own keys, and settle the naming so that an instance can be told which one to assume. State in AGENTS.md, and in SKILL.md where it bears on the loop, how an instance learns its identity, so that falling back to a shared name is a visible error rather than the path of least resistance.\n\nMake the review discipline checkable. For any implementation carried through the loop, the projection should be able to show whether the fingerprint of the reviewing actor differs from the fingerprint of the implementing actor, and a review report signed by the implementer should be distinguishable at a glance rather than only by someone who remembers who did the work. Decide whether that is a projector distinction, a warning at write time, or a stated limit; the failure to avoid is the one recorded in the assert this rests on, where the whole chain forms correctly and the record still cannot answer whether the review was independent.\n\nDecide the lifecycle. Whether instance identities are durable roster members or provisioned and revoked per engagement, what role-revoke means for one, and whether a retired instance identity should remain visible as a principal that once acted. Do not let the roster fill with abandoned names that no projection distinguishes from live ones.\n\nKeep custody honest. Every actor key currently sits in one local directory readable by any process on the machine, so instance identities are separated by convention and not by isolation. Either state that plainly where identities are documented, or change it; do not let the roster imply a separation that the filesystem does not provide.\n\nObtain independent exact-head review before merge, from an actor whose fingerprint differs from the implementer — which is the rule this request exists to make checkable.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}